\f1\b\fs28 \cf0 Likely biases to watch\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 Your 
\f1\b Machiavellianism score is the most obvious \'93monitor\'94 signal
\f0\b0 , particularly because it sits alongside relatively high ethical leadership and humility.\
That combination can sometimes produce a subtle tension:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 \'93I know how the system works\'94
\f0\b0  can be a strength, but under pressure it can become 
\f1\b \'93I know how to manoeuvre people through the system.\'94
\f0\b0 \
Similarly, high humility can become counterproductive if it turns into:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 reluctance to claim legitimate authority,\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 over-accommodation,\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 delaying a necessary confrontation,\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 assuming others' motives are better than the evidence supports.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 High empathy can also have a shadow side: 
\f1\b over-weighting immediate interpersonal discomfort
\f0\b0  and under-weighting a difficult but necessary organisational decision.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs28 \cf0 Potential workplace triggers\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 The most useful triggers to monitor are probably not \'93bad situations\'94 in general, but situations involving:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 Status threat:
\f0\b0  being challenged publicly, corrected, ignored, or undermined.\

\f1\b Loss of control:
\f0\b0  unclear ownership, political manoeuvring, sudden changes, or someone bypassing agreed processes.\

\f1\b Perceived unfairness:
\f0\b0  seeing someone rewarded despite poor behaviour, or watching standards applied inconsistently.\

\f1\b Repeated non-performance:
\f0\b0  when empathy and patience have been used repeatedly without improvement.\

\f1\b Moral frustration:
\f0\b0  situations where you believe the right thing is obvious but others appear to be acting opportunistically.\
Those are the contexts in which a normally ethical, empathic leader can become more tactical, rigid, sarcastic, withdrawn, or controlling.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa321\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs48 \cf0 2. Top 3 behavioural risks to monitor\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 These are deliberately phrased as 
\f1\b observable behaviours
\f0\b0 , not personality judgments.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs28 \cf0 1. Becoming overly tactical in conflict\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 Watch for:
\f0\b0  selectively sharing information, testing people rather than speaking directly, building informal alliances before addressing the issue, or framing communication mainly around controlling the outcome.\

\f1\b Early warning sign:
\f0\b0  you notice yourself thinking, 
\f2\i \'93I need to manage this person\'94
\f0\i0  rather than 
\f2\i \'93I need to address this problem.\'94
\f0\i0 \

\f1\b Better alternative:
\f0\b0  state the substantive issue, your reasoning, and the decision criteria explicitly before using influence tactics.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs28 \cf0 2. Becoming sharper or more dismissive under repeated frustration\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 Watch for:
\f0\b0  clipped responses, sarcasm, interrupting, excessive correction, public criticism, or visibly enjoying the fact that an opponent has been proven wrong.\

\f1\b Early warning sign:
\f0\b0  your goal shifts from 
\f1\b resolving the problem
\f0\b0  to 
\f1\b making a point
\f0\b0 .\

\f1\b Better alternative:
\f0\b0  move difficult feedback into a private setting, describe the behaviour and impact, and avoid commentary about the person's character or motives.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs28 \cf0 3. Letting empathy or humility delay necessary accountability\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 This is the \'93opposite-side\'94 risk in your profile.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 Watch for:
\f0\b0  repeatedly giving extra chances, softening feedback until the message becomes unclear, avoiding a difficult decision because it feels harsh, or taking too much responsibility yourself.\

\f1\b Early warning sign:
\f0\b0  you have had the same conversation several times without a change in behaviour.\

\f1\b Better alternative:
\f0\b0  combine compassion with a clear standard, consequence, owner, and review date.\
A useful principle is:\

\f1\b Empathy changes how you hold the boundary; it does not necessarily remove the boundary.
\f0\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa321\partightenfactor0

