\f1\b\fs48 \cf0 5. Short workplace scripts\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf0 Seeking feedback\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 \'93I\'92m working on how I lead under pressure. What is one behaviour I should keep, and one I should change?\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs28 \cf0 Pausing before a reactive decision\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 \'93Let me take a moment before I respond. I want to make sure I\'92m reacting to the facts rather than the frustration.\'94\
Or, in a meeting:\
\'93I have a strong reaction to that. Let me check my assumptions before I respond.\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs28 \cf0 Giving credit\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 \'93I want to make sure the contribution is properly recognised. [Name] did the key work on this, and my role was mainly to support and coordinate it.\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs28 \cf0 Repairing harm\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 \'93I handled that poorly. I interrupted you and made the discussion more difficult than it needed to be. I\'92m sorry. I\'92d like to hear your perspective and correct the way I handled it.\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs28 \cf0 Responding ethically to conflict\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 \'93I don\'92t think we need to agree personally, but we do need a fair process. Let\'92s separate the facts, the competing interests, and the decision criteria.\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs28 \cf0 When tempted to use organisational politics\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 \'93What would the transparent version of this conversation look like?\'94\
That question is particularly useful for the 
\f1\b Machiavellianism/ethical leadership tension
\f0\b0  in your results.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
