\f1\b\fs48 \cf0 6. Questions to ask yourself before applying any suggestion\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 Before changing your behaviour in a specific workplace, consider:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls7\ilvl0
\f1\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 What is the actual organisational context?
\f0\b0  A tactic that is appropriate in a highly political organisation may be unnecessary or counterproductive in a high-trust team.\
\ls7\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Is there a real power imbalance here?
\f0\b0  \'93Just be direct\'94 is not equally safe for a junior employee and a senior executive.\
\ls7\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Could this behaviour be mistaken for weakness, avoidance, or indecision in my role?
\f0\b0  Humility should not require abandoning legitimate authority.\
\ls7\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	4	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Am I trying to improve the outcome, protect a relationship, or reduce my own discomfort?
\f0\b0  Those are different goals.\
\ls7\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	5	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Would I recommend this same behaviour to a colleague I respect?
\f0\b0 \
\ls7\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	6	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Would I be comfortable describing my reasoning to the people affected by the decision?
\f0\b0 \
\ls7\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	7	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 What evidence would tell me that the experiment is working?
\f0\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa321\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs48 \cf0 7. Final caution\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 These results should be treated as 
\f1\b reflection prompts, not a diagnosis or a fixed description of who you are
\f0\b0 . In particular, scores on constructs such as narcissism, Machiavellianism, psychopathy, and sadism can be strongly affected by the questionnaire's wording, scoring method, social-desirability effects, and reference population. Without the instrument's norms, cut-offs, and reliability data, it would be inappropriate to label any score as inherently \'93healthy\'94 or \'93pathological.\'94\
The most constructive use of your results is to ask:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 \'93Which behaviours become more likely for me under certain conditions, and what safeguards help me choose differently?\'94
\f0\b0 \
Your strongest apparent safeguards are 
\f1\b humility, ethical orientation, and empathy
\f0\b0 . The development opportunity is not to suppress strategic thinking or strong standards, but to ensure that 
\f1\b influence remains transparent, accountability remains clear, and conflict does not become personal
\f0\b0 .\
And when using feedback or assessment data involving colleagues, keep the same standard you would want for yourself: 
\f1\b privacy, consent where appropriate, dignity, and no inference about someone's character from a score alone.
\f0\b0 \
